Run these commands from the [ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/user-guide/quickstart'))
checkout using Bazel 9.3.0.

> # [**Run** Generate a response]($block.collapsible(true).id('run-an-llm-example').attrs('bazel-recipe'))
>
> **Before you run.** Request access to Llama 3.2 1B Instruct on Hugging Face.
> Authenticate with `bazel run //tools/hf -- auth login` or set `HF_TOKEN`.
> See [Environment variables]($link.page('zml/cli-reference/environment-variables')) for credentials.
>
> > []($block.attrs('bazel-recipe-example'))
> >
> > ```sh
> > bazel run //examples/llm -- \
> >   --model=hf://meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct \
> >   --prompt='What is the capital of France?'
> > ```
> >
> > **Expected result** The startup log shows the platform and attention
> > backend, followed by generated text.
>
> See [Bazel and executable argument syntax]($link.page('zml/cli-reference').ref('run-an-llm-example'))
> and [LLM example flags]($link.page('zml/cli-reference').ref('llm-example-flags'))
> to adapt this command.
>
> > # [Run on NVIDIA CUDA]($block.collapsible(false).attrs('bazel-recipe-variant'))
> >
> > Use a compatible NVIDIA device and CUDA driver. Enable CUDA and disable
> > CPU before the separator.
> >
> > > []($block.attrs('bazel-recipe-example'))
> > >
> > > ```sh
> > > bazel run --@zml//platforms:cuda=true --@zml//platforms:cpu=false \
> > >   //examples/llm -- \
> > >   --model=hf://meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct \
> > >   --prompt='What is the capital of France?'
> > > ```
> > >
> > > **Expected result** The startup log shows CUDA before generation.

> # [**Test** Run the ZML test target]($block.collapsible(false).id('test-zml').attrs('bazel-recipe'))
>
> Use the checkout's default backend. This recipe uses `--test_output=all`
> to show logs from passing tests. See
> [Bazel options and defaults]($link.page('zml/cli-reference').ref('select-a-build-or-profiling-configuration')).
>
> > []($block.attrs('bazel-recipe-example'))
> >
> > ```sh
> > bazel test --test_output=all //zml:test
> > ```
> >
> > **Expected result** `//zml:test` reports `PASSED` when successful.

> # [**Profile** Capture a Perfetto trace]($block.collapsible(false).id('profile-an-llm-example').attrs('bazel-recipe'))
>
> **Before you run.** Use the model access and credentials from [Run]($link.ref('run-an-llm-example')).
> The process needs write access under `/tmp/xprof`.
>
> > []($block.attrs('bazel-recipe-example'))
> >
> > ```sh
> > bazel run //examples/llm -- \
> >   --model=hf://meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct \
> >   --prompt='What is the capital of France?' \
> >   --profile
> > ```
> >
> > **Expected result** Open the `profiling.trace.json` file listed after
> > `Profile dumped` in the log.
>
> The example takes `--profile` and `--prompt` after `--`. To use a Bazel
> profiler wrapper, select a [named configuration]($link.page('zml/cli-reference').ref('select-a-build-or-profiling-configuration'))
> before the separator.

> # [**Package** Bundle the executable and runfiles]($block.collapsible(false).id('package-a-build-for-a-different-host').attrs('bazel-recipe'))
>
> **Destination.** Use a Linux x86-64 host with a compatible NVIDIA device
> and driver. Install a tool that can extract Zstandard-compressed archives.
>
> > []($block.attrs('bazel-recipe-example'))
> >
> > ```sh
> > bazel build --config=release \
> >   --platforms=@zml//platforms:linux_amd64 \
> >   --@zml//platforms:cuda=true --@zml//platforms:cpu=false \
> >   //examples/llm:archive
> > ```
> >
> > **Expected artifact** `bazel-bin/examples/llm/archive.tar.zst` contains
> > the executable and runfiles.
>
> Copy the archive to the destination and extract it. Run `./examples/llm/llm`
> from the extracted tree with the model arguments. Keep the runfiles next to
> the executable. For `//examples/mnist:archive`, see the
> [MNIST deployment instructions](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/docs/howtos/deploy_on_server.md)
> for weight and image data paths.

